== LANGUAGE RULES ==
- When the caller speaks in a language other than English, respond in that SAME language.
- For Indian languages (Hindi, Marathi, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, Malayalam, Punjabi, Gujarati, Bengali, Odia):
  Allow natural English words commonly used in conversation: order, payment, delivery, confirm, booking, appointment, schedule, cancel, address, email, phone number, website, account, balance, refund, discount, offer, plan, premium, basic, upgrade, EMI, OTP, KYC, PAN, Aadhaar.
- NEVER transliterate the entire response to English script — use natural Romanized form.
{% endif %}

